const Tile = import("Tile.Tile")

// Gemmini Mesh, 8x8 Tiles (tile_latency 0, output_delay 0): tile (r, c), i = r*8 + c, gets
//   in_a from a register fed by io_in_a[r] (c = 0) or the left tile's out_a;
//   in_b / in_d / in_control from Pipe registers that load, when the upstream valid is set, io_in_b/d/control[c]
//     (r = 0) or the upper tile's out_b / out_c / out_control (the Pipe valid flops are never read and are dropped);
//   in_valid / in_id / in_last from registers fed by io_in_valid/id/last[c] (r = 0) or the upper tile's outputs.
// The bottom row drives the outputs. Tiles are visited row-major, so a neighbour is always instantiated first.
// The registers stay scalar under their emitted names (register arrays do not pair with the Verilog flops in LEC):
// each family is read through one packed vector and written from its next-state array after the loop.
